# TSG v2: every API call, ready to send (docs/DEBUGGING.md). Needs the REST Client extension.
# Send a call: click "Send Request" above it, or put the cursor in it and press Ctrl+Alt+R. The answer opens beside
# it, with the status, the headers (X-Request-Id) and the body.
# Which TSG: the laptop by default. For UAT press Ctrl+Alt+E and choose "uat" (its address: .vscode/settings.json).
# Your key and identity come from debug/.env (copy debug/.env.example first). Admin calls ask for the admin key each
# time and never store it.

@apiKey = {{$dotenv TSG_API_KEY}}
@userId = {{$dotenv TSG_USER_ID}}
@entityId = {{$dotenv TSG_ENTITY_ID}}
@tenantId = {{$dotenv TSG_TENANT_ID}}
@runId = {{$dotenv TSG_RUN_ID}}

### 1. Health: is the API process answering? Expect: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### 2. Ready: can it reach MongoDB, SQL Server, Redis and a worker on every queue? Expect: 200
# A 503 answer says which part is missing.
GET {{baseUrl}}/ready

### 2b. Metrics: the Prometheus numbers (what Grafana reads). Expect: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/metrics

### 3. Admin: mint an API key. Expect: 201
# Asks for the admin key. Copy "api_key" from the answer into debug/.env as TSG_API_KEY: it is shown only once.
# @prompt adminKey The admin key (CII_ADMIN_API_KEY in .env on the laptop, .env.uat for UAT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tsg/api-clients
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
X-User-Id: {{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "{{userId}}-{{$timestamp}}", "description": "minted from debug/tsg.http"}

### 4. Admin: list the active API keys (never shows keys). Expect: 200
# @prompt adminKey The admin key (CII_ADMIN_API_KEY in .env on the laptop, .env.uat for UAT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tsg/api-clients?active=true
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}

### 5. Check my key and headers work. Expect: 404
# 404 "Session 'check-my-key' does not exist." means TSG accepted your key and headers (no run has that id).
# 401 means the key or a header is wrong; 422 means a header breaks a rule.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/sessions/check-my-key/events
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-User-Id: {{userId}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entityId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}

### 6a. Error example: no identity headers. Expect: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/sessions/any-run/events

### 6b. Error example: a wrong API key. Expect: 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/sessions/any-run/events
X-API-Key: tsg_wrong
X-User-Id: {{userId}}
X-Entity-Id: {{entityId}}
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}

### 6c. Error example: an entity id that is not a number. Expect: 422
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/sessions/any-run/events
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-User-Id: {{userId}}
X-Entity-Id: abc
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}

### 6d. Error example: a run of another entity. Expect: 403
# Needs TSG_RUN_ID in debug/.env: run the task 'TSG: make a test run (laptop)' first.
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/sessions/{{runId}}/events
X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
X-User-Id: {{userId}}
X-Entity-Id: 999999
X-Tenant-Id: {{tenantId}}

### 6e. Error example: an address that does not exist. Expect: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/nothing-here

### 6f. Error example: the wrong method. Expect: 405
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/health

### 6g. Error example (admin): a key name of only spaces. Expect: 422
# @prompt adminKey The admin key (CII_ADMIN_API_KEY in .env on the laptop, .env.uat for UAT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tsg/api-clients
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "   "}

### 7. Send your own request id: TSG keeps it, so your id and TSG's logs match. Expect: 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/health
X-Request-Id: my-debug-0001

### 8. Admin: revoke an API key. Expect: 200
# Asks for the admin key and the key's client_id (from request 3 or 4). The answer shows "active": false.
# @prompt adminKey The admin key (CII_ADMIN_API_KEY in .env on the laptop, .env.uat for UAT)
# @prompt clientId The client_id of the key to revoke
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tsg/api-clients/{{clientId}}/revoke
X-Admin-Key: {{adminKey}}
X-User-Id: {{userId}}
